{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>A prince of Elohim.</b> They answered him point by point. You said 'a stranger and resident' — it is not so, but rather 'a prince of Elohim are you.' And what you asked, to acquire a burial estate — 'lest they dig there' (פן יחרשו בו): in the choicest of our graves (במבחר קברנו), in the select grave in which they bury the nobles. <b>Bury your dead.</b> And it is an honor for you to seek yourself a place in the choicest of our graves. <b>Any man of us his grave</b> (איש ממנו את קברו): even a grave specially designated for him in his lifetime."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:23.656133500Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}